      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "HEARD OF HIM (6) showed promise as a juvenile, winning 1 of his 3 starts, and sent for a spell after a fair effort in town at Rosehill in June. He has trialled up twice, and will have the services of top hoop Keagan Latham. Hard to beat, especially if the track is wet. COCO DIOR (7) was well placed to win a 50K maiden at Moruya just over 2 weeks ago, and she has the scope to go right on with the job. EL QASABI (3) has needed time to mature, and he was a deserving maiden winner when ending his last prep over 1500m at Kembla Grange. Having Aaron Bullock in the saddle is a strong lead, and he is likely to be ready after a couple of quiet tune-up trials. Follow the markets. ZOUBOY (2) won his debut as expected last season, and he has been taken along patiently since then. He looks to be very promising, and has to be respected fresh up in this. TAKE FLIGHT (8) resumes from a spell, and she can make her presence felt, so keep her safe in all combos.",
